# requires: arch=arm64 -threaded

# pKVM Slice 3a: KVM_ENABLE_CAP(KVM_CAP_ARM_PROTECTED_VM, INFO) on a protected VM, as a composite.
# syz_kvm_pvm_info builds a bit-31 protected VM and issues the INFO cap with a valid info buffer, all in
# C. INFO always succeeds on a protected VM with a valid pointer (pkvm.c:638-647), so the call returns 0.
# The firmware_size it writes is the GLOBAL pkvm_firmware_mem (non-zero on N90, which has a preinstalled
# pvmfw), not per-VM, so this test does not assert the size. N90 acceptance: the call returns 0; no WARN.

r0 = openat$kvm(0xffffffffffffff9c, &AUTO='/dev/kvm\x00', 0x2, 0x0)
syz_kvm_pvm_info$arm64(r0)
